## Data Quality — Mandatory from Clean Layer

Every table from the **clean** layer onwards must have a corresponding data quality file in `data_quality/{layer}/{table}.yml`.

**Inmetro YAML** (Error vs Warning, check placement, custom keys, size floors, `has_size_variation`): always apply `.cursor/rules/people/people_data_quality.mdc`. When creating or editing `data_quality/*.yml` files, **also apply** `.cursor/rules/data_quality_tests.mdc` for Inmetro **syntax**. Use `alert_channel: PEOPLE_ALERTS` and `table_name` fully qualified (e.g. `dw_employee_details.fact_absence_requests`).

### Ad-hoc SQL and pre-merge DQ validation — Trino first

**People lake tables are available in Trino.** Use **Trino** (`trino` skill / Trino MCP) as the **default** for triaging Inmetro alerts, validating `custom` constraints from `data_quality/**/*.yml`, or any ad-hoc query against People schemas (`datalake_people*`, `datalake_pin_*`, `datalake_gsheets_people*`, `dw_*` People domains) — no need to pre-check `list_tables` before trusting it.

Fall back to the **Databricks CLI** against production below, or to an ad-hoc **EMR cluster** via the **`emr-run`** skill (`.cursor/skills/emr-run/SKILL.md`, role **`emr-people-prod`** for People data), only for a **brand-new** table that has not been deployed to prod yet (e.g. same-PR table, not merged/deployed), or if a Trino query unexpectedly errors with `TABLE_NOT_FOUND` / `SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND`.

#### Workspace and authentication

`PROD` and `quintoandar_prod` below are **local Databricks CLI / Unity Catalog names** in `~/.databrickscfg` and the prod workspace — not pipeline environment strings. The **ConfigurationService** rule (never hardcode `"prod"` in DAG SQL or Spark jobs) does not apply to this operator runbook.

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| **Workspace host** | `https://dbc-931ee6e0-6803.cloud.databricks.com` |
| **Workspace ID** | `4531937035440038` |
| **CLI profile** | `PROD` in `~/.databrickscfg` (`auth_type = databricks-cli`) |
| **OAuth** | `https://dbc-931ee6e0-6803.cloud.databricks.com/oidc` |
| **Unity Catalog (prod)** | `quintoandar_prod` — prefix SQL with `USE CATALOG quintoandar_prod;` |

**Token env conflicts:** If `databricks` returns `more than one authorization method configured`, unset `DATABRICKS_TOKEN`, `DATABRICKS_HOST`, and `DATABRICKS_USERNAME` for the session:

```bash
env -u DATABRICKS_TOKEN -u DATABRICKS_HOST -u DATABRICKS_USERNAME databricks … -p PROD
```

#### People test clusters — use whichever is RUNNING

Two all-purpose clusters are available for People ad-hoc work. **Pick the one in `RUNNING` state**; do not start a cluster unless the user explicitly asks.

| Cluster name | Cluster ID | HTTP path (SQL) |
|--------------|--------------|-----------------|
| Tests - People Analytics | `0119-124615-zurgst68` | `sql/protocolv1/o/4531937035440038/0119-124615-zurgst68` |
| Tests - AE @ People | `1107-173945-rr76o3kf` | `sql/protocolv1/o/4531937035440038/1107-173945-rr76o3kf` |

List current state:

```bash
env -u DATABRICKS_TOKEN -u DATABRICKS_HOST -u DATABRICKS_USERNAME \
  databricks clusters list -p PROD -o json \
  | python3 -c "import json,sys; ids={'0119-124615-zurgst68','1107-173945-rr76o3kf'}; [print(c['cluster_id'], c['cluster_name'], c['state']) for c in json.load(sys.stdin) if c['cluster_id'] in ids]"
```

#### Run SQL via Commands API

Use the cluster **ID** (not the HTTP path) with the Databricks REST API through the CLI:

```bash
CLUSTER_ID="<running-cluster-id>"   # e.g. 0119-124615-zurgst68
PROFILE="PROD"
DBX="env -u DATABRICKS_TOKEN -u DATABRICKS_HOST -u DATABRICKS_USERNAME databricks"

# 1) Create SQL context
CTX=$($DBX api post /api/1.2/contexts/create -p "$PROFILE" -o json \
  --json "{\"clusterId\": \"$CLUSTER_ID\", \"language\": \"sql\"}" | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['id'])")

# 2) Execute (always set catalog for People tables)
CMD=$($DBX api post /api/1.2/commands/execute -p "$PROFILE" -o json \
  --json "{\"clusterId\": \"$CLUSTER_ID\", \"contextId\": \"$CTX\", \"language\": \"sql\", \"command\": \"USE CATALOG quintoandar_prod; SELECT COUNT(*) FROM dw_compensation.dim_job\"}" \
  | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['id'])")

# 3) Poll until status is Finished
$DBX api get "/api/1.2/commands/status?clusterId=$CLUSTER_ID&contextId=$CTX&commandId=$CMD" -p "$PROFILE" -o json
```

For **Inmetro `custom` constraints**, run the inner `SELECT` from the YAML `constraint` block (expect `COUNT(*) = 0`). JDBC/ODBC clients can use the HTTP path from the table above with `AuthMech=3` and a personal access token — prefer the CLI workflow for agents.

